                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "79623bb4-424c-3327-81d2-b73110a8eb81",
                        "entry_id": "0dbac2c5-4faa-3912-b5d6-299bb681cbb3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A male given name from the Germanic languages."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b62c3e8-8422-46a7-824e-21fa887b5be5",
                                "sense_id": "79623bb4-424c-3327-81d2-b73110a8eb81",
                                "text": "Whitmore. And so am I; my name is Walter Whitmore. / How now! why start'st thou? what! doth death affright?\nSuffolk. Thy name affrights me, in whose sound is death. / A cunning man did calculate my birth, / And told me that by Water I should die. / Yet let not this make thee be bloody-minded; / Thy name is - Gaultier, being rightly sounded."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "895eb0d2-b476-4d7c-bae6-afc593f42406",
                                "sense_id": "79623bb4-424c-3327-81d2-b73110a8eb81",
                                "text": "And with some appellations, the contrary applies. Like Walter, for instance. You can't be Walter in a pram. You can't be Walter until you're about seventy-five in my view."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "54683a77-2530-4313-8cd3-7abc50321cd0",
                                "sense_id": "79623bb4-424c-3327-81d2-b73110a8eb81",
                                "text": "Walter complained about the assault and isolation of the volunteers. Two policemen immediately grabbed him and dragged him to the punishment cells."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d722eb82-8790-46bb-bdcd-30e6a9a8e1ae",
                                "sense_id": "79623bb4-424c-3327-81d2-b73110a8eb81",
                                "text": "On the podcast, Gaines and his co-host Walter Weekes (Fresh), regularly refer to women as “hoes” or 304s (304 on an upside-down calculator looks like the word “hoe”)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
